title: Agents that work at once
pid: 5d657386-0c30-442d-8357-d6b3dabb1075
body: |2-
  Each agent works in a git worktree of its own, with its own 'target/',
  never shared or symlinked: a shared one lets one agent's build
  replace the binary another's tests are running. Each sets
  'SKG_FOR_AI_TEST_PORT' to a port of its own before running the AI
  reader's tests or the suite, and no other agent may use the port
  after it, where those tests start a second server; their default,
  1793, collides.
  None runs 'git stash': worktrees share one stash list, and Jeff's
  stashes are in it. None runs 'pkill' or 'killall' by name, which
  kills other agents' servers and Jeff's; each kills only PIDs it
  started. An agent lands its branch under one lock ('flock'),
  holding it while it rebases on 'main', runs the whole suite and
  fast-forwards 'main'; without the lock, two agents each test a
  'main' the other is about to change.
